    {
      "id": "g02",
      "title": {
        "t": "ich möchte – ich mag",
        "s": "\"I'd like\" and \"I like\""
      },
      "explain": "**ich möchte** means *I would like*. It's the polite way to ask for something – in a café, in a shop or at home: **Ich möchte eine Suppe, bitte.**\n**ich mag** means *I like* – in general: **Ich mag Reis.** To say you don't like something, use **kein** / **keine**: Ich mag **keine** Bananen.\nNote: **ich** and **er / sie / es** have the same form, with no **-t**: ich möchte, er möchte – ich mag, sie mag.",
      "table": [
        [
          "ich",
          "möchte",
          "mag"
        ],
        [
          "du",
          "möchtest",
          "magst"
        ],
        [
          "er / sie / es",
          "möchte",
          "mag"
        ],
        [
          "wir",
          "möchten",
          "mögen"
        ],
        [
          "Sie",
          "möchten",
          "mögen"
        ]
      ],
      "examples": [
